{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1819","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Willy-nilly, Crack, Into Release!"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1024 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have long dreamed of working in a large IT company and finally got a job there. You have studied all existing modern technologies for a long time and are ready to apply all your knowledge in practice. But then you sit down at your desk and see a sheet of paper with the company's motto printed in large letters: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abcdabcdabcdabcd..."}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The company's motto contains four main principles— "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (Willi), "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (Nilli), "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (Crack), "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (Release). Therefore, you consider strings of length $$$n$$$ consisting of these four Latin letters. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Unordered"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" pairs of letters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"da"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in this motto are adjacent, so we will call such pairs of symbols "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". So, if you are given a string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$, and it is known that the unordered pair of symbols $$$\\{ x, y \\}$$$ is good, then you can perform one of the following operations on the string:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$s_n = x$$$, then you are allowed to replace this symbol with $$$y$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if there exists $$$1 \\le i \\lt n$$$ such that $$$s_i = x$$$ and $$$s_{i+1} = \\ldots = s_n = y$$$, then you are allowed to replace the $$$i$$$-th symbol of the string with $$$y$$$, and all subsequent symbols with $$$x$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, the string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bacdd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be replaced with one of the strings "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bacda"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bacdc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"badcc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aac"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be replaced with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aad"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A non-empty sequence of operations for the string $$$s$$$ will be called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"correct"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if the following two conditions are met:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" after performing all operations, the string becomes $$$s$$$ again, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" no string, except for $$$s$$$, will occur more than once during the operations. At the same time, the string $$$s$$$ can occur exactly twice - before the start of the operations and after performing all operations. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now we are ready to move on to the problem statement! You have a set of strings that is initially empty. Then, each of $$$q$$$ queries adds another string $$$t_i$$$ to the set, or removes the string $$$t_i$$$ from the set. After each query, you need to output the minimum and maximum size of a correct sequence of operations in which each word occurs at least once. The choice of the initial string $$$s$$$ is up to you."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$q$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 20$$$, $$$1 \\le q \\le 100\\,000$$$) — the length of the strings under consideration and the number of queries to modify the set of strings."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$q$$$ lines contains a string $$$t_i$$$ ($$$\\lvert t_i \\rvert = n$$$). All strings consist of characters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". If the string $$$t_i$$$ was not in the set before the query, it is added to the set, otherwise it is removed from the set."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each of the $$$q$$$ queries, output two integers: the minimum and maximum size of a correct sequence of operations in which each word from the set appears at least once."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there is no sequence of operations that satisfies the condition of the problem, output a single number $$$-1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 4\naa\nac\ndd\nac\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 12\n4 4\n-1\n12 12\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 2\nacc\nbdd\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 44\n28 44\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's consider the first test example."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" After the first query, the set of important words is equal to $$$\\{$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\}$$$, the minimum sequence of actions has the following form: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". The maximum sequence of actions that fits is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ba"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"da"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ad"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" After the second query, the set of important words is equal to $$$\\{$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa, ac"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\}$$$. The minimum and maximum sequences of actions are: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ac"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ad"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" After the third query, the set of important words is equal to $$$\\{$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa, ac, dd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\}$$$. There is no sequence of actions that fits the condition, so $$$-1$$$ should be outputted. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" After the fourth query, the set of important words is equal to $$$\\{$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa, dd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\}$$$. The minimum and maximum sequences of actions are as follows: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ba"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dc"}],"kind":"contai